{"name":"Black Ribbon","hex":"#484c51","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"ribbon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, narrow strip of material used for decoration of clothing or the hair or gift wrapping.","An awareness ribbon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with ribbon.","To stripe or streak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ribbon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"A black ribbon is a symbol of remembrance or mourning. It is often worn or put on a public display to express consolation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Black_Ribbon.svg/330px-Black_Ribbon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_ribbon"},{"title":"Ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"A ribbon is a thin band of material, typically cloth but also plastic or sometimes metal, used primarily as decorative binding and tying. Cloth ribbons are made of natural materials such as silk, cotton, and jute and of synthetic materials, such as polyester, nylon, and polypropylene. Ribbon is used for useful, ornamental, and symbolic purposes. Cultures around the world use ribbon in their hair, around the body, and as ornament on non-human animals, buildings, and packaging. Some popular fabrics used to make ribbons are satin, organza, sheer, silk, velvet, and grosgrain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg/330px-Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribbon"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/2010_Olympic_Winter_Games_Opening_Ceremony_-_Georgia_entering_cropped.jpg/500px-2010_Olympic_Winter_Games_Opening_Ceremony_-_Georgia_entering_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/2010_Olympic_Winter_Games_Opening_Ceremony_-_Georgia_entering_cropped.jpg/500px-2010_Olympic_Winter_Games_Opening_Ceremony_-_Georgia_entering_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A black ribbon may be put on a flag, as on the Georgian flag at the 2010 Winter Olympics opening ceremony.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2010_Olympic_Winter_Games_Opening_Ceremony_-_Georgia_entering_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Melanoma_Awareness_Ribbon_alternative.jpg/500px-Melanoma_Awareness_Ribbon_alternative.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or